            <description><![CDATA[<!-- Release notes for Snappy 1.2.
     Committed here so the site can serve them, and copied into the appcast by
     scripts/build-direct.sh so Sparkle embeds them in the update dialog. The
     Keep this aligned with v1.2.md; Sparkle embeds this version in its update
     dialog while the GitHub release uses the Markdown version. -->
<!doctype html>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>Snappy 1.2</title>
<style>
  :root {
    color-scheme: light dark;
    --ink: #16181b;
    --mid: #63696f;
    --surface: #ffffff;
    --hair: #dcdfdf;
    --alert-bg: #fff6e8;
    --alert-edge: #e0a341;
    --alert-ink: #6b4708;
    --code-bg: #f1f3f3;
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root {
      --ink: #e8e9eb;
      --mid: #9aa0a6;
      --surface: #191b1f;
      --hair: #2a2d32;
      --alert-bg: #2a2110;
      --alert-edge: #b5822f;
      --alert-ink: #f0d08a;
      --code-bg: #23262b;
    }
  }
  body {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 16px 18px 22px;
    font: 13px/1.55 -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "SF Pro Text", system-ui, sans-serif;
    color: var(--ink);
    background: var(--surface);
  }
  h1 { font-size: 17px; margin: 0 0 2px; letter-spacing: -0.01em; }
  h2 { font-size: 13px; margin: 20px 0 6px; letter-spacing: 0.02em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--mid); }
  p { margin: 0 0 9px; }
  ul { margin: 0 0 9px; padding-left: 19px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 5px; }
  .version-date { color: var(--mid); margin: 0 0 4px; }
  .alert {
    border: 1px solid var(--alert-edge);
    border-left-width: 3px;
    background: var(--alert-bg);
    color: var(--alert-ink);
    border-radius: 6px;
    padding: 11px 13px;
    margin: 14px 0 4px;
  }
  .alert h2 { margin-top: 0; color: inherit; }
  .alert p:last-child, ul:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .path { background: var(--code-bg); border-radius: 4px; padding: 1px 5px; font-size: 12px; white-space: nowrap; }
  hr { border: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--hair); margin: 18px 0; }
</style>

<h1>Snappy 1.2</h1>
<p class="version-date">Window placement for macOS</p>

<h2>New</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    <strong>Report an Issue.</strong> The Snappy menu now has a
    <span class="path">Report an Issue…</span> item. It collects the handful of
    facts that actually determine whether window placement can work — whether
    macOS trusts Snappy, whether Input Monitoring is granted, whether Secure
    Input is currently blocking every application from seeing the keyboard, and
    whether the keyboard hook is really receiving events — and opens a prefilled
    issue with them. Hold Option to copy the report without opening a browser.
  </li>
  <li>
    Those are exactly the conditions that produce “Snappy opens but nothing
    happens”, and none of them are visible from the outside. Having them in the
    first message saves a long exchange.
  </li>
  <li>
    The report covers Snappy, its permissions and its own settings. It does not
    include window titles, the applications you are running, or any file path
    beyond Snappy itself.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Fixed</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    The download link at <span class="path">getsnappy.fyi/Snappy.zip</span>
    works again. It had been serving the website instead of a download since the
    site moved.
  </li>
</ul>

<h2>Notes</h2>
<ul>
  <li>
    Nothing about placement, permissions or your settings changes in this
    release. If 1.1 is working for you, 1.2 changes only what happens when it
    isn’t.
  </li>
</ul>
]]></description>
